  "task": {
    "objective": "Use shared hedges, blankets, hoe, watering can and moving pollinator to grow six original plants, harvest them and carry their produce to the village.",
    "natural_termination": "Natural end when every bed is harvested or dead and no active produce remains in the world. This includes completed delivery and crop-loss exhaustion; otherwise truncate at tick 180.",
    "interaction": "Moving a hedge alters wind shelter, moving sunlight shadows, walking space and the insect route. A blanket preserves a bed against frost while preventing growth, pollination, tending and harvesting until physically removed. Shared single tools and one-item hands require labor and inventory handoffs.",
    "observation_access": "Fully observable village. Every role receives identical flattened clock, ground map, all worker/bed/object/insect/facility positions, plot labels, crop stages/moisture/soil/frost/alive/harvested/pollination/shelter/shade/cover state, object kinds/holders/deployment/blanket assignment/water, insect route index/direction, weather phase and delivery counters. Inactive produce slots remain explicit in the native observation but are not drawn as active objects. All public scene attributes are contained in the same observation."
  },
